  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Multidimensional Integrated Stabilization Mission Mali (MINUSMA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Multidimensional Integrated Stabilization Mission in Mali (Mission multidimensionnelle int&#xe9;gr&#xe9;e des Nations unies pour la stabilisation au Mali, MINUSMA) is a United Nations peacekeeping mission in Mali. MINUSMA was established on 25 April 2013 by UN Security Council Resolution 2100 to stabilise the country after the Tuareg rebellion (2012). It was officially deployed on 1 July. Funding under this activity represents Australia&apos;s assessed contribution to the operation.</narrative>
  </description>
